window.DEEP = [{"id":"warfare","title":"Spiritual Warfare","icon":"sword","words":"spiritual warfare battle enemy devil satan attack armor armour stronghold oppression fight","intro":"The Bible says the Christian life includes a real struggle, but not against people. The enemy is Satan and the forces under him, and he has already been defeated by Christ at the cross. We do not fight for victory; we fight from victory, using the armor and weapons God supplies.","points":["The battle is spiritual, not against flesh and blood (Ephesians 6:12).","Christ disarmed the rulers and authorities at the cross and triumphed over them (Colossians 2:15).","The armor of God: truth, righteousness, the gospel of peace, faith, salvation, the Word of God, and prayer (Ephesians 6:14-18).","Submit to God first, then resist the devil, and he will flee (James 4:7).","Our weapons are not carnal but mighty through God to pull down strongholds, including wrong thoughts that exalt themselves against the knowledge of God (2 Corinthians 10:3-5).","Stay sober and watchful, without fearing the devil and without being fascinated by him (1 Peter 5:8-9)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Ephesians 6:10-12","text":"Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might. Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil. For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places."},{"ref":"Ephesians 6:13-18","text":"Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand. Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness; And your feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace; Above all, taking the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked. And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God: Praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit, and watching thereunto with all perseverance and supplication for all saints;"},{"ref":"James 4:7","text":"Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you."},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 10:3-5","text":"For though we walk in the flesh, we do not war after the flesh: (For the weapons of our warfare are not carnal, but mighty through God to the pulling down of strong holds;) Casting down imaginations, and every high thing that exalteth itself against the knowledge of God, and bringing into captivity every thought to the obedience of Christ;"},{"ref":"Colossians 2:15","text":"And having spoiled principalities and powers, he made a shew of them openly, triumphing over them in it."},{"ref":"1 John 4:4","text":"Ye are of God, little children, and have overcome them: because greater is he that is in you, than he that is in the world."},{"ref":"1 Peter 5:8-9","text":"Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour: Whom resist stedfast in the faith, knowing that the same afflictions are accomplished in your brethren that are in the world."},{"ref":"Revelation 12:11","text":"And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death."},{"ref":"Luke 10:19","text":"Behold, I give unto you power to tread on serpents and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy: and nothing shall by any means hurt you."},{"ref":"Isaiah 54:17","text":"No weapon that is formed against thee shall prosper; and every tongue that shall rise against thee in judgment thou shalt condemn. This is the heritage of the servants of the LORD, and their righteousness is of me, saith the LORD."}],"reflect":["Which piece of the armor do I most often leave off?","What lie am I believing that Scripture clearly contradicts?","Who can I ask to stand with me in prayer this week?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Putting on the armor","x":"Father in heaven, I come to You in the name of Jesus Christ. Thank You that You have already defeated the enemy at the cross. Today I put on the whole armor of God. I fasten the belt of truth, I put on the breastplate of righteousness, I wear the shoes of the gospel of peace, I lift the shield of faith, I put on the helmet of salvation and I take up the sword of the Spirit, which is Your Word.\n\nI submit myself to You, Lord. In the authority of Jesus, I resist the devil, and I believe he must flee. I renounce fear, deception, confusion and every lie that has tried to take root in my mind. Strengthen me in the Lord and in the power of His might. Fill me afresh with Your Holy Spirit. Thank You that greater is He that is in me than he that is in the world. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{"t":"Covering my home and family","x":"Lord Jesus, I place my home, my family and everything You have given me under Your care. Be a wall of fire around us and the glory in our midst. Let Your peace rule in every room. Keep out every spirit of fear, strife, sickness and confusion. Send Your angels to guard us in all our ways. Teach us to love one another, to forgive quickly and to pray together. We will serve the Lord. In Jesus' name, Amen."}],"declare":["I am more than a conqueror through Christ who loves me.","No weapon formed against me shall prosper.","Greater is He that is in me than he that is in the world.","I overcome by the blood of the Lamb and the word of my testimony.","I have authority in Jesus' name, and I use it humbly, in prayer and in the Word."],"care":"Not every struggle is a spiritual attack. Sickness, grief, anxiety and depression are often real health matters that need a doctor or counselor as well as prayer. Seek a trusted pastor and also medical help when you need it."},{"id":"purity","title":"Lust and Purity","icon":"shield","words":"lust purity sexual temptation pornography porn adultery immorality desire flesh pure holy","intro":"The Bible treats sexual purity seriously because it protects the heart, the body and relationships. Jesus taught that lust begins in the heart. The good news is that God does not only command purity, He gives power, forgiveness and a way back to those who fall.","points":["Jesus said that looking with lust is adultery of the heart (Matthew 5:27-28), so the battle starts in the eyes and mind.","Flee sexual immorality; it is a sin against your own body, which is the temple of the Holy Spirit (1 Corinthians 6:18-20).","Guard your heart above everything, for it is the wellspring of life (Proverbs 4:23).","Walk in the Spirit and you will not carry out the desires of the flesh (Galatians 5:16).","No temptation is beyond what you can bear, and God always provides a way out (1 Corinthians 10:13).","Confession brings cleansing: He is faithful and just to forgive (1 John 1:9). Shame is not the way back; grace is."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Matthew 5:27-28","text":"Ye have heard that it was said by them of old time, Thou shalt not commit adultery: But I say unto you, That whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 6:18-20","text":"Flee fornication. Every sin that a man doeth is without the body; but he that committeth fornication sinneth against his own body. What? know ye not that your body is the temple of the Holy Ghost which is in you, which ye have of God, and ye are not your own? For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God's."},{"ref":"Proverbs 4:23","text":"Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life."},{"ref":"Galatians 5:16","text":"This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 10:13","text":"There hath no temptation taken you but such as is common to man: but God is faithful, who will not suffer you to be tempted above that ye are able; but will with the temptation also make a way to escape, that ye may be able to bear it."},{"ref":"Job 31:1","text":"I made a covenant with mine eyes; why then should I think upon a maid?"},{"ref":"Psalm 51:10","text":"Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me."},{"ref":"2 Timothy 2:22","text":"Flee also youthful lusts: but follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace, with them that call on the Lord out of a pure heart."},{"ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:3-5","text":"For this is the will of God, even your sanctification, that ye should abstain from fornication: That every one of you should know how to possess his vessel in sanctification and honour; Not in the lust of concupiscence, even as the Gentiles which know not God:"},{"ref":"1 John 1:9","text":"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness."}],"reflect":["What doors (screens, places, people, habits) do I need to close?","Who is my accountability partner, and when do we speak?","What do I turn to when I am lonely, tired or stressed?"],"prayers":[{"t":"A prayer for a pure heart","x":"Holy Father, You see my heart and You know my struggle. I confess that I have given in to lust and impure thoughts. I do not hide it from You any longer. Forgive me, cleanse me from all unrighteousness and wash me in the blood of Jesus.\n\nCreate in me a clean heart, O God, and renew a right spirit within me. I make a covenant with my eyes. I turn away from what is not pure, and I choose to fix my mind on whatever is true, honorable, right and pure. Break every chain of habit, every secret and every lie that says I cannot change. Fill the empty places in me with Your presence. Give me wise friends who will walk with me, and the courage to ask for help. I receive Your power to walk in the Spirit. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{"t":"In the moment of temptation","x":"Lord Jesus, I am being tempted right now and I run to You. You were tempted in every way, yet without sin, so You understand. I say no to this, and I turn my eyes and my thoughts to You. Give me strength to walk away. Thank You for the way of escape that You promised. I choose You. Amen."}],"declare":["My body is the temple of the Holy Spirit.","I walk in the Spirit and I will not obey the desires of the flesh.","I have made a covenant with my eyes.","There is no condemnation for me in Christ Jesus.","God is making me pure, and He is faithful to finish what He started."],"care":"If this is a long struggle or has become an addiction, please talk to a pastor and consider a counselor who understands addiction. Asking for help is a sign of strength, not failure."},{"id":"repentance","title":"Repentance","icon":"broken","words":"repentance repent turn confess forgive sorry guilt return prodigal restore","intro":"Repentance means a real change of mind that leads to a change of direction: turning away from sin and turning back to God. It is not only feeling bad. True repentance is a gift from God, and it always leads to forgiveness and joy, never to rejection.","points":["Repentance is a change of mind and direction, produced by godly sorrow (2 Corinthians 7:10).","God is ready to forgive: if we confess, He is faithful and just to forgive and cleanse (1 John 1:9).","The kindness of God leads us to repentance (Romans 2:4).","Jesus said there is joy in heaven over one sinner who repents (Luke 15:7).","Repentance bears fruit: changed actions, making things right where possible (Luke 3:8).","God does not despise a broken and contrite heart (Psalm 51:17)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"2 Corinthians 7:10","text":"For godly sorrow worketh repentance to salvation not to be repented of: but the sorrow of the world worketh death."},{"ref":"1 John 1:9","text":"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness."},{"ref":"Romans 2:4","text":"Or despisest thou the riches of his goodness and forbearance and longsuffering; not knowing that the goodness of God leadeth thee to repentance?"},{"ref":"Luke 15:7","text":"I say unto you, that likewise joy shall be in heaven over one sinner that repenteth, more than over ninety and nine just persons, which need no repentance."},{"ref":"Luke 15:20","text":"And he arose, and came to his father. But when he was yet a great way off, his father saw him, and had compassion, and ran, and fell on his neck, and kissed him."},{"ref":"Psalm 51:17","text":"The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt not despise."},{"ref":"Acts 3:19","text":"Repent ye therefore, and be converted, that your sins may be blotted out, when the times of refreshing shall come from the presence of the Lord;"},{"ref":"Proverbs 28:13","text":"He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy."},{"ref":"Isaiah 55:7","text":"Let the wicked forsake his way, and the unrighteous man his thoughts: and let him return unto the LORD, and he will have mercy upon him; and to our God, for he will abundantly pardon."},{"ref":"Joel 2:13","text":"And rend your heart, and not your garments, and turn unto the LORD your God: for he is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repenteth him of the evil."}],"reflect":["Is there something I have hidden from God that I need to name?","Where do I need to go back and make things right with someone?","Do I believe that God really welcomes me home?"],"prayers":[{"t":"A prayer of repentance","x":"Merciful Father, I come to You with a heavy heart. I have sinned against You, against others and against myself. I do not make excuses. I name my sin before You: (say it honestly to God). I am truly sorry, and by Your grace I turn away from it.\n\nThank You that Jesus died for this sin, and that Your mercy is bigger than my failure. Wash me, cleanse me and forgive me, as You promised. Remove the guilt and the shame. Restore to me the joy of Your salvation, and uphold me with a willing spirit. Show me what to do to make things right. Help me walk in a new way, step by step, leaning on Your strength. Thank You that You are running toward me with open arms. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{"t":"Lord, search me","x":"Search me, O God, and know my heart. Try me and know my thoughts. See if there is any wicked way in me, and lead me in the way everlasting. Show me what I cannot see in myself, and give me the courage to face it with You. Amen."}],"declare":["I am forgiven, not because I deserve it, but because Jesus paid for it.","The blood of Jesus cleanses me from all sin.","God remembers my sin no more, and I will not carry it any longer.","I turn from what is wrong and I walk toward what is right."],"care":"If guilt feels crushing or you are thinking of harming yourself, please tell someone you trust or contact your local emergency services right away. God's forgiveness is real, and so is help."},{"id":"newbirth","title":"Born Again","icon":"dove","words":"born again new birth salvation saved regeneration spirit new creation convert accept jesus","intro":"Jesus told Nicodemus, \"Ye must be born again.\" This is not self-improvement. It is a new beginning that only God can give: a new heart and a new life through the Holy Spirit, received by faith in Jesus Christ.","points":["No one can see the kingdom of God unless they are born again, of water and the Spirit (John 3:3-5).","We are saved by grace through faith, as a gift, not by works (Ephesians 2:8-9).","Whoever receives Jesus and believes in His name becomes a child of God (John 1:12-13).","If anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation; the old has passed away (2 Corinthians 5:17).","Confess with your mouth that Jesus is Lord and believe in your heart that God raised Him from the dead (Romans 10:9-10).","The Spirit bears witness with our spirit that we are children of God (Romans 8:16)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"John 3:3","text":"Jesus answered and said unto him, Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God."},{"ref":"John 3:5-8","text":"Jesus answered, Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born of water and of the Spirit, he cannot enter into the kingdom of God. That which is born of the flesh is flesh; and that which is born of the Spirit is spirit. Marvel not that I said unto thee, Ye must be born again. The wind bloweth where it listeth, and thou hearest the sound thereof, but canst not tell whence it cometh, and whither it goeth: so is every one that is born of the Spirit."},{"ref":"John 3:16","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life."},{"ref":"John 1:12-13","text":"But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name: Which were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God."},{"ref":"Ephesians 2:8-9","text":"For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast."},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 5:17","text":"Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new."},{"ref":"Romans 10:9-10","text":"That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved. For with the heart man believeth unto righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made unto salvation."},{"ref":"Romans 8:16","text":"The Spirit itself beareth witness with our spirit, that we are the children of God:"},{"ref":"Titus 3:5","text":"Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Ghost;"},{"ref":"Ezekiel 36:26","text":"A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh."}],"reflect":["Can I point to a time when I trusted Christ for myself?","What has changed in me since I began following Jesus?","Who needs to hear about this new life?"],"prayers":[{"t":"A prayer to be born again","x":"Lord Jesus Christ, I believe that You are the Son of God, that You died on the cross for my sins and that You rose again from the dead. I admit that I am a sinner and that I cannot save myself. Today I turn from my sin and I turn to You. I open the door of my heart and I receive You as my Lord and Savior.\n\nThank You for forgiving me and making me a child of God. Give me a new heart and fill me with Your Holy Spirit. Write my name in Your book of life. Help me to follow You every day, to read Your Word, to pray and to find other believers who will help me grow. From today, I belong to You. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{"t":"For someone who is not yet saved","x":"Father, I lift up (name) to You. Open their eyes to see Jesus. Soften their heart and draw them by Your Spirit. Send people into their life who will speak the truth in love. Let this be the season of their salvation. Thank You that You are not willing that any should perish. Amen."}],"declare":["I am born again, not of corruptible seed but of incorruptible, by the Word of God.","I am a child of God.","I am a new creation: the old has passed away, behold all things have become new.","My name is written in the Lamb's book of life."],"care":"If you prayed this prayer for the first time, tell a believer you trust and find a Bible-teaching church. Growing in faith is easier together."},{"id":"sin","title":"Sin and Its Power","icon":"chain","words":"sin sinner transgression iniquity guilt bondage wages death fall adam","intro":"The Bible says that sin is not only wrong actions but a power that separates us from God and enslaves us. Every person has sinned. But where sin increased, grace increased all the more, and Christ has broken sin's power over those who trust Him.","points":["All have sinned and fall short of the glory of God (Romans 3:23).","The wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus (Romans 6:23).","Sin promises freedom but makes a person a slave (John 8:34), and the Son sets free indeed (John 8:36).","Sin shall not have dominion over you, because you are under grace (Romans 6:14).","Our sins separate us from God, but Christ bore them on the cross (Isaiah 59:2; 1 Peter 2:24).","Even the believer still struggles, but there is now no condemnation in Christ Jesus (Romans 8:1)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Romans 3:23","text":"For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;"},{"ref":"Romans 6:23","text":"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord."},{"ref":"John 8:34","text":"Jesus answered them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Whosoever committeth sin is the servant of sin."},{"ref":"John 8:36","text":"If the Son therefore shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed."},{"ref":"Romans 6:14","text":"For sin shall not have dominion over you: for ye are not under the law, but under grace."},{"ref":"Isaiah 59:2","text":"But your iniquities have separated between you and your God, and your sins have hid his face from you, that he will not hear."},{"ref":"1 Peter 2:24","text":"Who his own self bare our sins in his own body on the tree, that we, being dead to sins, should live unto righteousness: by whose stripes ye were healed."},{"ref":"Romans 8:1","text":"There is therefore now no condemnation to them which are in Christ Jesus, who walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit."},{"ref":"James 1:14-15","text":"But every man is tempted, when he is drawn away of his own lust, and enticed. Then when lust hath conceived, it bringeth forth sin: and sin, when it is finished, bringeth forth death."},{"ref":"Romans 5:20","text":"Moreover the law entered, that the offence might abound. But where sin abounded, grace did much more abound:"}],"reflect":["Which sin keeps returning in my life, and what feeds it?","Am I trying to overcome it by willpower, or by walking with Jesus?","Do I hide, or do I bring it into the light?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Breaking the power of sin","x":"Father, I thank You that Jesus took my sin on the cross and that sin no longer has the final word over me. I confess that I have sinned and I have let sin rule in an area of my life. I call it what it is. I turn from it.\n\nIn the name of Jesus, I break every agreement I have made with sin and with the lies behind it. By the blood of Jesus I am forgiven and set free. Sin shall not have dominion over me, for I am under grace. Lead me not into temptation, and deliver me from evil. Give me a hunger for righteousness. Help me to walk in the light and to be honest with You and with others. In Jesus' name, Amen."}],"declare":["The wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life.","Sin shall not have dominion over me.","Whom the Son sets free is free indeed.","I have been bought with a price, and I belong to God."],"care":"If sin has become a pattern you cannot break alone, bring someone alongside you: a pastor, a mature believer or a counselor."},{"id":"death","title":"Death","icon":"candle","words":"death die dying grief funeral mourning loss afterlife mortality grave","intro":"Death is an enemy, and the Bible does not pretend otherwise. Death came through sin, and Jesus wept at a grave. But for those who trust in Christ, death is not the end: He has taken away its sting and promised that those who believe in Him will live even though they die.","points":["Death entered the world through sin, but Christ has abolished death (Romans 5:12; 2 Timothy 1:10).","Jesus said, \"I am the resurrection and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live\" (John 11:25).","To be absent from the body is to be present with the Lord (2 Corinthians 5:8).","We do not grieve as those who have no hope (1 Thessalonians 4:13-14).","The last enemy to be destroyed is death (1 Corinthians 15:26).","God sees the death of His faithful ones as precious (Psalm 116:15), and He will wipe away every tear (Revelation 21:4)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"John 11:25-26","text":"Jesus said unto her, I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live: And whosoever liveth and believeth in me shall never die. Believest thou this?"},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 5:8","text":"We are confident, I say, and willing rather to be absent from the body, and to be present with the Lord."},{"ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:13-14","text":"But I would not have you to be ignorant, brethren, concerning them which are asleep, that ye sorrow not, even as others which have no hope. For if we believe that Jesus died and rose again, even so them also which sleep in Jesus will God bring with him."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:26","text":"The last enemy that shall be destroyed is death."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:55-57","text":"O death, where is thy sting? O grave, where is thy victory? The sting of death is sin; and the strength of sin is the law. But thanks be to God, which giveth us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ."},{"ref":"Psalm 116:15","text":"Precious in the sight of the LORD is the death of his saints."},{"ref":"Psalm 23:4","text":"Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me."},{"ref":"Revelation 21:4","text":"And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away."},{"ref":"Hebrews 9:27","text":"And as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment:"},{"ref":"Romans 8:38-39","text":"For I am persuaded, that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor powers, nor things present, nor things to come, Nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord."}],"reflect":["Am I ready to meet God? What would I want to settle?","How am I grieving, and who is walking with me?","What would change if I truly believed death is not the end?"],"prayers":[{"t":"In grief and loss","x":"Lord of life, my heart is broken. I miss the one I have lost, and the pain is real. Thank You that You are close to the brokenhearted and that You wept with Mary and Martha. Hold me when I cannot hold myself. Let me cry without shame and rest without guilt.\n\nThank You for the hope of the resurrection and that death does not have the last word. Comfort me with the comfort of Your Holy Spirit. Surround me with people who love me. Give me strength for each day, one day at a time. Help me honor the memory of the one I love by living well. Receive them into Your presence, and one day bring us together again. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{"t":"Facing my own mortality","x":"Father, my days are in Your hands. Teach me to number my days so that I gain a heart of wisdom. I put my trust in Jesus, who defeated death. Help me to live without fear, to forgive, to love and to be ready. When my time comes, let me go home in peace. Amen."}],"declare":["Though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil, for You are with me.","Death is swallowed up in victory.","Jesus is the resurrection and the life, and in Him I will live.","Nothing can separate me from the love of God in Christ Jesus."],"care":"Grief takes time. If you cannot eat, sleep or function for weeks, or you feel you cannot go on, please reach out to a doctor, a counselor or your local emergency services."},{"id":"life","title":"Life: Abundant and Eternal","icon":"tree","words":"life abundant eternal living purpose spirit alive resurrection everlasting","intro":"Jesus said, \"I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly.\" Real life is knowing God. It begins now, in Christ, and it never ends. The Bible calls this eternal life, and it is a gift received by faith, not something earned.","points":["Eternal life is knowing the only true God and Jesus Christ whom He sent (John 17:3).","Jesus came that we may have life and have it abundantly (John 10:10).","God so loved the world that whoever believes in the Son will not perish but have eternal life (John 3:16).","He who has the Son has life; he who does not have the Son does not have life (1 John 5:11-12).","Our life is hidden with Christ in God (Colossians 3:3).","Choose life: love the Lord, obey Him and hold fast to Him, for He is your life (Deuteronomy 30:19-20)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"John 10:10","text":"The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly."},{"ref":"John 17:3","text":"And this is life eternal, that they might know thee the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom thou hast sent."},{"ref":"John 3:16","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life."},{"ref":"1 John 5:11-12","text":"And this is the record, that God hath given to us eternal life, and this life is in his Son. He that hath the Son hath life; and he that hath not the Son of God hath not life."},{"ref":"John 14:6","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me."},{"ref":"Colossians 3:3","text":"For ye are dead, and your life is hid with Christ in God."},{"ref":"Deuteronomy 30:19-20","text":"I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live: That thou mayest love the LORD thy God, and that thou mayest obey his voice, and that thou mayest cleave unto him: for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land which the LORD sware unto thy fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, to give them."},{"ref":"Galatians 2:20","text":"I am crucified with Christ: nevertheless I live; yet not I, but Christ liveth in me: and the life which I now live in the flesh I live by the faith of the Son of God, who loved me, and gave himself for me."},{"ref":"Psalm 16:11","text":"Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore."},{"ref":"Romans 6:4","text":"Therefore we are buried with him by baptism into death: that like as Christ was raised up from the dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in newness of life."}],"reflect":["What does an abundant life look like to me, and does it match Jesus' words?","Where am I settling for less than the life God offers?","How will I use the time I have today?"],"prayers":[{"t":"For life in abundance","x":"Lord Jesus, thank You that You came to give me life, and life to the full. Forgive me for the times I have settled for less: for a busy life instead of a full life, or a comfortable life instead of a life with You. Fill me with Your Spirit. Let Your joy be my strength and Your peace guard my heart.\n\nShow me the path of life, and let me live each day in Your presence, where there is fullness of joy. Help me to live for the things that last: to love You, to love people and to make a difference for Your kingdom. Thank You for the gift of eternal life that begins now. In Jesus' name, Amen."}],"declare":["I have life, and I have it abundantly.","I have passed from death to life.","The life I now live, I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave Himself for me.","I will choose life."],"care":""},{"id":"heaven","title":"Heaven","icon":"heaven","words":"heaven eternity paradise glory new jerusalem home afterlife streets gold","intro":"Heaven is where God dwells, and the Bible promises that His people will be with Him forever. Scripture speaks of a place without death, mourning, crying or pain, and of a renewed heaven and earth. Our greatest joy there will be seeing Jesus and living in His presence.","points":["Jesus is preparing a place for His followers and will come back to receive them (John 14:2-3).","In God's presence is fullness of joy, and at His right hand are pleasures forevermore (Psalm 16:11).","God will wipe away every tear; there will be no more death, sorrow, crying or pain (Revelation 21:3-4).","Our citizenship is in heaven, and we await a Savior who will transform us (Philippians 3:20-21).","Eye has not seen nor ear heard what God has prepared for those who love Him (1 Corinthians 2:9).","Store up treasures in heaven, where nothing can destroy them (Matthew 6:19-21)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"John 14:2-3","text":"In my Father's house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you. And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come again, and receive you unto myself; that where I am, there ye may be also."},{"ref":"Revelation 21:1-4","text":"And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea. And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband. And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and God himself shall be with them, and be their God. And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away."},{"ref":"Revelation 22:3-5","text":"And there shall be no more curse: but the throne of God and of the Lamb shall be in it; and his servants shall serve him: And they shall see his face; and his name shall be in their foreheads. And there shall be no night there; and they need no candle, neither light of the sun; for the Lord God giveth them light: and they shall reign for ever and ever."},{"ref":"Psalm 16:11","text":"Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore."},{"ref":"Philippians 3:20-21","text":"For our conversation is in heaven; from whence also we look for the Saviour, the Lord Jesus Christ: Who shall change our vile body, that it may be fashioned like unto his glorious body, according to the working whereby he is able even to subdue all things unto himself."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 2:9","text":"But as it is written, Eye hath not seen, nor ear heard, neither have entered into the heart of man, the things which God hath prepared for them that love him."},{"ref":"Matthew 6:19-21","text":"Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and where thieves break through and steal: But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt, and where thieves do not break through nor steal: For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also."},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 5:1","text":"For we know that if our earthly house of this tabernacle were dissolved, we have a building of God, an house not made with hands, eternal in the heavens."},{"ref":"Hebrews 11:16","text":"But now they desire a better country, that is, an heavenly: wherefore God is not ashamed to be called their God: for he hath prepared for them a city."},{"ref":"Luke 23:43","text":"And Jesus said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, To day shalt thou be with me in paradise."}],"reflect":["How does the hope of heaven change how I handle suffering today?","What treasure am I storing up, and where?","Who do I want to meet there, and who needs an invitation?"],"prayers":[{"t":"A prayer of heavenly hope","x":"Father, thank You that You have prepared a place for those who love You. When I am tired, remind me that this world is not my home. When I am grieving, remind me that there will be no more tears. Fix my eyes on Jesus, who has gone ahead of me.\n\nHelp me to set my mind on things above and to live as a citizen of heaven. Teach me to store up treasure where moth and rust cannot destroy. Let the hope of seeing You face to face make me patient, brave and generous. Come quickly, Lord Jesus. Until then, use me here. In Jesus' name, Amen."}],"declare":["My citizenship is in heaven.","I have an inheritance that can never perish, spoil or fade.","One day I will see Jesus face to face.","In His presence is fullness of joy."],"care":""},{"id":"hell","title":"Hell and Judgment","icon":"fire","words":"hell judgment damnation lake of fire eternal punishment condemnation wrath hades gehenna","intro":"Jesus spoke about hell more than anyone else in the Bible, and He did so with deep seriousness and love. Scripture teaches that there is a judgment, and that separation from God is real. Believers differ in how they understand its details, but all agree on the main message: God does not want anyone to perish, and Jesus took the judgment on Himself so that we need not face it.","points":["It is appointed for people to die once, and after that comes judgment (Hebrews 9:27).","God does not want anyone to perish, but all to come to repentance (2 Peter 3:9).","There is now no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus (Romans 8:1).","Whoever believes in the Son is not condemned, but whoever does not believe is condemned already (John 3:18).","Jesus warned about eternal fire prepared for the devil and his angels (Matthew 25:41), and about the broad road that leads to destruction (Matthew 7:13).","The wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life (Romans 6:23)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Hebrews 9:27","text":"And as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment:"},{"ref":"2 Peter 3:9","text":"The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance."},{"ref":"John 3:18","text":"He that believeth on him is not condemned: but he that believeth not is condemned already, because he hath not believed in the name of the only begotten Son of God."},{"ref":"Romans 8:1","text":"There is therefore now no condemnation to them which are in Christ Jesus, who walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit."},{"ref":"Matthew 7:13-14","text":"Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat: Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it."},{"ref":"Matthew 25:41","text":"Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels:"},{"ref":"Revelation 20:11-15","text":"And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them. And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works. And the sea gave up the dead which were in it; and death and hell delivered up the dead which were in them: and they were judged every man according to their works. And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death. And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire."},{"ref":"Mark 9:43-48","text":"And if thy hand offend thee, cut it off: it is better for thee to enter into life maimed, than having two hands to go into hell, into the fire that never shall be quenched: Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched. And if thy foot offend thee, cut it off: it is better for thee to enter halt into life, than having two feet to be cast into hell, into the fire that never shall be quenched: Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched. And if thine eye offend thee, pluck it out: it is better for thee to enter into the kingdom of God with one eye, than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire: Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched."},{"ref":"Romans 6:23","text":"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord."},{"ref":"Ezekiel 33:11","text":"Say unto them, As I live, saith the Lord GOD, I have no pleasure in the death of the wicked; but that the wicked turn from his way and live: turn ye, turn ye from your evil ways; for why will ye die, O house of Israel?"}],"reflect":["Am I certain of my own salvation, based on Christ and not my effort?","Who in my life do I need to share the gospel with, with love and urgency?","What does it say about God's love that Jesus took the judgment for me?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Deliver me from judgment","x":"Righteous and merciful God, I fear You and I trust You. I know that I deserve judgment, and I thank You that Jesus took my place on the cross. I put my trust in Him alone for forgiveness and eternal life. I do not trust my own goodness.\n\nThank You that there is no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus. Give me a heart that burns for people who do not know You. Help me to speak with love and truth. Let me live each day in the light of eternity. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{"t":"Prayer for the lost","x":"Lord, You are not willing that any should perish. I pray for my family, friends and neighbours who do not yet know You. Open their eyes, soften their hearts and send workers into their path. Give me courage and compassion to share the good news. Amen."}],"declare":["There is no condemnation for me in Christ Jesus.","I have passed from death to life.","Jesus has delivered me from the wrath to come.","I will tell others about the hope that is in me."],"care":"If fear about hell is troubling you, trust that those who come to Jesus He will never cast out (John 6:37). Talk to a pastor about assurance of salvation."},{"id":"demons","title":"Demons and Deliverance","icon":"cloud","words":"demons demon devil deliverance exorcism evil spirit unclean spirit oppression possession occult witchcraft curse darkness","intro":"The Bible teaches that evil spirits are real, that they are under the authority of Jesus and that they are limited and defeated. Jesus cast out demons with a word, and He gave His followers authority in His name. The Bible also warns us against curiosity about the occult and against blaming everything on demons.","points":["Demons are fallen spirits who follow Satan; they are real but limited (Jude 6; James 2:19).","Jesus has all authority, and the demons obeyed Him and trembled before Him (Luke 4:36; Mark 1:27).","Believers have authority in Jesus' name, used humbly and in dependence on God (Luke 10:17-20).","The Bible forbids the occult: sorcery, divination, mediums and spiritism (Deuteronomy 18:10-12).","Test the spirits, for many false prophets have gone out into the world (1 John 4:1).","Do not rejoice in power over spirits; rejoice that your name is written in heaven (Luke 10:20)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Mark 1:23-27","text":"And there was in their synagogue a man with an unclean spirit; and he cried out, Saying, Let us alone; what have we to do with thee, thou Jesus of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art, the Holy One of God. And Jesus rebuked him, saying, Hold thy peace, and come out of him. And when the unclean spirit had torn him, and cried with a loud voice, he came out of him. And they were all amazed, insomuch that they questioned among themselves, saying, What thing is this? what new doctrine is this? for with authority commandeth he even the unclean spirits, and they do obey him."},{"ref":"Luke 10:17-20","text":"And the seventy returned again with joy, saying, Lord, even the devils are subject unto us through thy name. And he said unto them, I beheld Satan as lightning fall from heaven. Behold, I give unto you power to tread on serpents and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy: and nothing shall by any means hurt you. Notwithstanding in this rejoice not, that the spirits are subject unto you; but rather rejoice, because your names are written in heaven."},{"ref":"Luke 4:36","text":"And they were all amazed, and spake among themselves, saying, What a word is this! for with authority and power he commandeth the unclean spirits, and they come out."},{"ref":"Deuteronomy 18:10-12","text":"There shall not be found among you any one that maketh his son or his daughter to pass through the fire, or that useth divination, or an observer of times, or an enchanter, or a witch, Or a charmer, or a consulter with familiar spirits, or a wizard, or a necromancer. For all that do these things are an abomination unto the LORD: and because of these abominations the LORD thy God doth drive them out from before thee."},{"ref":"1 John 4:1-4","text":"Beloved, believe not every spirit, but try the spirits whether they are of God: because many false prophets are gone out into the world. Hereby know ye the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesseth that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is of God: And every spirit that confesseth not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is not of God: and this is that spirit of antichrist, whereof ye have heard that it should come; and even now already is it in the world. Ye are of God, little children, and have overcome them: because greater is he that is in you, than he that is in the world."},{"ref":"James 2:19","text":"Thou believest that there is one God; thou doest well: the devils also believe, and tremble."},{"ref":"Acts 19:13-16","text":"Then certain of the vagabond Jews, exorcists, took upon them to call over them which had evil spirits the name of the Lord Jesus, saying, We adjure you by Jesus whom Paul preacheth. And there were seven sons of one Sceva, a Jew, and chief of the priests, which did so. And the evil spirit answered and said, Jesus I know, and Paul I know; but who are ye? And the man in whom the evil spirit was leaped on them, and overcame them, and prevailed against them, so that they fled out of that house naked and wounded."},{"ref":"Mark 16:17","text":"And these signs shall follow them that believe; In my name shall they cast out devils; they shall speak with new tongues;"},{"ref":"Colossians 1:13","text":"Who hath delivered us from the power of darkness, and hath translated us into the kingdom of his dear Son:"},{"ref":"2 Timothy 1:7","text":"For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind."}],"reflect":["Have I opened any door to the occult (games, horoscopes, charms, mediums) that I need to close?","Am I giving the devil credit for things that are really about my own choices or health?","Who is my pastor or prayer partner I can call?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Prayer for deliverance and freedom","x":"Lord Jesus Christ, You have all authority in heaven and on earth. I come to You in humility and faith. I confess every sin, every involvement with the occult, and every door I have opened to darkness, knowingly or unknowingly. I repent and I close those doors in the name of Jesus.\n\nI renounce Satan and all his works. In the name of Jesus Christ, I command every spirit of fear, bondage, confusion and evil that is not of God to leave me now and go where Jesus sends you. You have no right here: I belong to Jesus, who bought me with His blood. Holy Spirit, fill every place that has been emptied. Give me a spirit of power, love and a sound mind. Thank You that You have delivered me from the dominion of darkness and brought me into the kingdom of Your beloved Son. In Jesus' name, Amen."},{"t":"Peace for my sleep","x":"Lord, I lie down in peace, for You alone make me dwell in safety. I rebuke every spirit of fear and every night terror in the name of Jesus. I fill my heart with Your Word and my mind with Your peace. Let me sleep, and let me wake with joy. Amen."}],"declare":["The One who is in me is greater than the one who is in the world.","God has not given me a spirit of fear, but of power, love and a sound mind.","He has delivered me from the power of darkness.","In the name of Jesus every knee shall bow."],"care":"Please do not try to handle serious oppression alone. Bring a trusted pastor or mature believers, and also see a doctor if there are signs of mental illness, because both prayer and medicine can help. Never be told to stop medication because of prayer."},{"id":"angels","title":"Angels","icon":"wings","words":"angels angel archangel michael gabriel heavenly host guardian cherubim seraphim messengers","intro":"Angels are real, created spiritual beings who serve God. The Bible shows them worshiping God, carrying His messages, protecting His people and carrying out His commands. We are never told to pray to angels or worship them; they point to God, and they serve those who will inherit salvation.","points":["Angels are ministering spirits sent to serve those who will inherit salvation (Hebrews 1:14).","God commands His angels to guard His people in all their ways (Psalm 91:11).","Angels brought messages: Gabriel to Mary and Zechariah, an angel to the shepherds (Luke 1:19, 26; 2:9-14).","Angels rejoice over one sinner who repents (Luke 15:10).","Do not worship angels (Colossians 2:18; Revelation 22:8-9).","Be kind to strangers, for some have unknowingly entertained angels (Hebrews 13:2)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Hebrews 1:14","text":"Are they not all ministering spirits, sent forth to minister for them who shall be heirs of salvation?"},{"ref":"Psalm 91:11-12","text":"For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways. They shall bear thee up in their hands, lest thou dash thy foot against a stone."},{"ref":"Psalm 34:7","text":"The angel of the LORD encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them."},{"ref":"Luke 2:9-14","text":"And, lo, the angel of the Lord came upon them, and the glory of the Lord shone round about them: and they were sore afraid. And the angel said unto them, Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people. For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord. And this shall be a sign unto you; Ye shall find the babe wrapped in swaddling clothes, lying in a manger. And suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly host praising God, and saying, Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men."},{"ref":"Luke 15:10","text":"Likewise, I say unto you, there is joy in the presence of the angels of God over one sinner that repenteth."},{"ref":"Daniel 10:12-13","text":"Then said he unto me, Fear not, Daniel: for from the first day that thou didst set thine heart to understand, and to chasten thyself before thy God, thy words were heard, and I am come for thy words. But the prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me one and twenty days: but, lo, Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me; and I remained there with the kings of Persia."},{"ref":"Matthew 18:10","text":"Take heed that ye despise not one of these little ones; for I say unto you, That in heaven their angels do always behold the face of my Father which is in heaven."},{"ref":"2 Kings 6:16-17","text":"And he answered, Fear not: for they that be with us are more than they that be with them. And Elisha prayed, and said, LORD, I pray thee, open his eyes, that he may see. And the LORD opened the eyes of the young man; and he saw: and, behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire round about Elisha."},{"ref":"Hebrews 13:2","text":"Be not forgetful to entertain strangers: for thereby some have entertained angels unawares."},{"ref":"Revelation 22:8-9","text":"And I John saw these things, and heard them. And when I had heard and seen, I fell down to worship before the feet of the angel which shewed me these things. Then saith he unto me, See thou do it not: for I am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren the prophets, and of them which keep the sayings of this book: worship God."}],"reflect":["Do I trust that God sends help I cannot see?","Have I been tempted to pray to angels instead of to God?","How can I be an encouraging messenger to someone today?"],"prayers":[{"t":"A prayer of thanks for God's protection","x":"Father, thank You that You rule over all things and that You send Your angels to guard those who love You. Thank You for the protection I have never seen and the times I was kept safe without knowing. Open my eyes, as You opened Elisha's servant's eyes, to know that those who are with us are more than those who are against us.\n\nI will not worship angels, but I worship You alone, God, with all the heavenly host. Guard my family on the roads, at home and at work. Teach me to trust You in every danger. Make me a blessing to strangers. In Jesus' name, Amen."}],"declare":["The angel of the Lord encamps around those who fear Him and delivers them.","God has given His angels charge over me to guard me in all my ways.","Those who are with us are more than those who are with them.","I worship God alone."],"care":""},{"id":"blood","title":"The Blood of Jesus and the Cross","icon":"drop","words":"blood of jesus cross calvary atonement redeemed sacrifice lamb cleanse covenant ransom","intro":"At the center of the Christian faith is the cross. Jesus shed His blood as the spotless Lamb of God, taking the penalty of our sin so that we could be forgiven, redeemed and brought near to God. The power of prayer and the confidence of the believer rest on what He finished there.","points":["Without the shedding of blood there is no forgiveness of sins (Hebrews 9:22).","We are redeemed not with silver or gold but with the precious blood of Christ (1 Peter 1:18-19).","The blood of Jesus cleanses us from all sin (1 John 1:7).","Through His blood we have boldness to enter the holy place (Hebrews 10:19).","The accuser is overcome by the blood of the Lamb (Revelation 12:11).","\"It is finished\" (John 19:30): the work is done and we receive it by faith."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Hebrews 9:22","text":"And almost all things are by the law purged with blood; and without shedding of blood is no remission."},{"ref":"1 Peter 1:18-19","text":"Forasmuch as ye know that ye were not redeemed with corruptible things, as silver and gold, from your vain conversation received by tradition from your fathers; But with the precious blood of Christ, as of a lamb without blemish and without spot:"},{"ref":"1 John 1:7","text":"But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin."},{"ref":"Hebrews 10:19-22","text":"Having therefore, brethren, boldness to enter into the holiest by the blood of Jesus, By a new and living way, which he hath consecrated for us, through the veil, that is to say, his flesh; And having an high priest over the house of God; Let us draw near with a true heart in full assurance of faith, having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience, and our bodies washed with pure water."},{"ref":"Revelation 12:11","text":"And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death."},{"ref":"John 19:30","text":"When Jesus therefore had received the vinegar, he said, It is finished: and he bowed his head, and gave up the ghost."},{"ref":"Isaiah 53:5","text":"But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed."},{"ref":"Romans 5:8-9","text":"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us. Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we shall be saved from wrath through him."},{"ref":"Ephesians 1:7","text":"In whom we have redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of sins, according to the riches of his grace;"},{"ref":"Colossians 1:20","text":"And, having made peace through the blood of his cross, by him to reconcile all things unto himself; by him, I say, whether they be things in earth, or things in heaven."}],"reflect":["Do I live as someone who is fully forgiven, or as someone still on trial?","What does it mean to me that He took my place?","How can I thank Him today?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Pleading the blood","x":"Lord Jesus, I thank You for the cross. Thank You for the blood You shed for me. Today I come to You with boldness, not because of my goodness but because of Yours. By Your blood I am forgiven, redeemed from the hand of the enemy and brought near to God.\n\nI cover my mind, my body, my home and my family with the blood of Jesus. Let every accusation against me fall silent. Wash my conscience from dead works so that I can serve the living God. I receive Your peace, which You made by the blood of Your cross. All glory and thanks to You, Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world. Amen."}],"declare":["I am forgiven by the blood of Jesus.","I am redeemed from the hand of the enemy.","I have been made righteous through Christ.","I enter God's presence with boldness through the blood of Jesus."],"care":""},{"id":"spirit","title":"The Holy Spirit and Power","icon":"flame","words":"holy spirit power anointing baptism filled gifts tongues fruit comforter helper guidance","intro":"The Holy Spirit is God with us: the Helper whom Jesus promised. He convicts us of sin, gives new birth, lives in every believer, produces the fruit of Christ-like character, and empowers us to witness and serve. Christians differ on some details of the Spirit's gifts, but all agree that we desperately need Him.","points":["The Spirit is the Helper, the Spirit of truth, who guides us into all truth (John 14:16-17; 16:13).","We receive power when the Holy Spirit comes upon us, to be Christ's witnesses (Acts 1:8).","Be filled with the Spirit, not drunk with wine (Ephesians 5:18).","The fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness and self-control (Galatians 5:22-23).","The Spirit helps us in our weakness and prays for us (Romans 8:26-27).","Do not grieve or quench the Spirit (Ephesians 4:30; 1 Thessalonians 5:19)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"John 14:16-17","text":"And I will pray the Father, and he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever; Even the Spirit of truth; whom the world cannot receive, because it seeth him not, neither knoweth him: but ye know him; for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you."},{"ref":"John 16:13","text":"Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will guide you into all truth: for he shall not speak of himself; but whatsoever he shall hear, that shall he speak: and he will shew you things to come."},{"ref":"Acts 1:8","text":"But ye shall receive power, after that the Holy Ghost is come upon you: and ye shall be witnesses unto me both in Jerusalem, and in all Judaea, and in Samaria, and unto the uttermost part of the earth."},{"ref":"Ephesians 5:18","text":"And be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit;"},{"ref":"Galatians 5:22-23","text":"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith, Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law."},{"ref":"Romans 8:26-27","text":"Likewise the Spirit also helpeth our infirmities: for we know not what we should pray for as we ought: but the Spirit itself maketh intercession for us with groanings which cannot be uttered. And he that searcheth the hearts knoweth what is the mind of the Spirit, because he maketh intercession for the saints according to the will of God."},{"ref":"Romans 8:11","text":"But if the Spirit of him that raised up Jesus from the dead dwell in you, he that raised up Christ from the dead shall also quicken your mortal bodies by his Spirit that dwelleth in you."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 12:7","text":"But the manifestation of the Spirit is given to every man to profit withal."},{"ref":"Luke 11:13","text":"If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children: how much more shall your heavenly Father give the Holy Spirit to them that ask him?"},{"ref":"Acts 2:1-4","text":"And when the day of Pentecost was fully come, they were all with one accord in one place. And suddenly there came a sound from heaven as of a rushing mighty wind, and it filled all the house where they were sitting. And there appeared unto them cloven tongues like as of fire, and it sat upon each of them. And they were all filled with the Holy Ghost, and began to speak with other tongues, as the Spirit gave them utterance."}],"reflect":["Where do I rely on my own strength instead of the Spirit?","Which fruit of the Spirit do I most need right now?","Am I listening for His quiet voice?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Come, Holy Spirit","x":"Heavenly Father, You promised to give the Holy Spirit to those who ask. I ask now. Holy Spirit, come and fill me afresh. Fill my mind with truth, my heart with love and my mouth with words that give life. Search me and cleanse me. I surrender every area of my life to You.\n\nGive me power to witness, courage to obey and wisdom to walk in Your ways. Grow Your fruit in me: love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness and self-control. Help me when I do not know how to pray. Make me sensitive to Your leading. Let my life glorify Jesus. In His name, Amen."}],"declare":["The Holy Spirit lives in me.","I am led by the Spirit of God.","I have power through the Holy Spirit to be a witness for Jesus.","The fruit of the Spirit is growing in my life."],"care":""},{"id":"strongholds","title":"Strongholds and Addictions","icon":"chain","words":"strongholds addiction addicted bondage stronghold habits alcohol drugs gambling freedom chains generational pattern","intro":"A stronghold is a pattern of thinking or behavior that has taken hold and seems impossible to break: addiction, anger, fear, or a lie about who you are. The Bible says God's weapons are powerful to pull down strongholds, and that \"whom the Son sets free is free indeed.\" Freedom usually comes through truth, honest confession, community and the power of Jesus, together.","points":["The weapons of our warfare are mighty to pull down strongholds (2 Corinthians 10:4).","Take every thought captive to obey Christ (2 Corinthians 10:5).","If the Son sets you free, you will be free indeed (John 8:36).","Truth sets us free: know it, believe it and live in it (John 8:32).","Confess your sins to one another and pray for one another, that you may be healed (James 5:16).","Bear one another's burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ (Galatians 6:2)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"2 Corinthians 10:4-5","text":"(For the weapons of our warfare are not carnal, but mighty through God to the pulling down of strong holds;) Casting down imaginations, and every high thing that exalteth itself against the knowledge of God, and bringing into captivity every thought to the obedience of Christ;"},{"ref":"John 8:32","text":"And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free."},{"ref":"John 8:36","text":"If the Son therefore shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed."},{"ref":"James 5:16","text":"Confess your faults one to another, and pray one for another, that ye may be healed. The effectual fervent prayer of a righteous man availeth much."},{"ref":"Galatians 6:1-2","text":"Brethren, if a man be overtaken in a fault, ye which are spiritual, restore such an one in the spirit of meekness; considering thyself, lest thou also be tempted. Bear ye one another's burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ."},{"ref":"Galatians 5:1","text":"Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Christ hath made us free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage."},{"ref":"Romans 12:2","text":"And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God."},{"ref":"Psalm 107:13-14","text":"Then they cried unto the LORD in their trouble, and he saved them out of their distresses. He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and brake their bands in sunder."},{"ref":"Isaiah 61:1","text":"The Spirit of the Lord GOD is upon me; because the LORD hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound;"},{"ref":"Proverbs 28:13","text":"He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy."}],"reflect":["What lie sits underneath my struggle?","Who knows about this, and who should?","What first small step toward freedom can I take today?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Break every chain","x":"Lord Jesus, You came to proclaim freedom to the captives and to set the oppressed free. I bring You this chain: (name it honestly). I admit that I cannot break it on my own, and I ask for Your power. I confess the ways I have fed it, hidden it and excused it.\n\nIn the name of Jesus I renounce every lie behind this stronghold. I break every agreement with it. I receive Your forgiveness, Your truth and Your strength. Replace the lie with Your truth, and the craving with Your presence. Lead me to the right people and help: a pastor, a counselor, a recovery group, a doctor. Give me courage to take each step. Thank You that whom the Son sets free is free indeed. Amen."}],"declare":["I am free in Christ, and I will not submit again to a yoke of slavery.","The truth has set me free.","My mind is being renewed by the Word of God.","I do not walk alone: God and His people are with me."],"care":"Addictions often need professional help, such as a doctor, counselor or a recovery programme, alongside prayer. Please do not stop medication without a doctor's advice. If you are in danger, call your local emergency services."},{"id":"fear","title":"The Fear of the Lord","icon":"shield","words":"fear of the lord reverence awe holy holiness wisdom respect","intro":"The fear of the Lord is not terror but reverence: seeing God as He is, holy, powerful and loving, and responding with awe and obedience. The Bible calls it the beginning of wisdom and a fountain of life. It frees us from the fear of people and of the future.","points":["The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 9:10).","It leads to life and rest, and keeps us from evil (Proverbs 14:27; 16:6).","The Lord takes pleasure in those who fear Him and hope in His mercy (Psalm 147:11).","To fear the Lord is to hate evil (Proverbs 8:13).","Perfect love casts out fear (1 John 4:18): we fear God as children who are loved.","Work out your salvation with fear and trembling, for God is at work in you (Philippians 2:12-13)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Proverbs 9:10","text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy is understanding."},{"ref":"Proverbs 14:27","text":"The fear of the LORD is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death."},{"ref":"Proverbs 8:13","text":"The fear of the LORD is to hate evil: pride, and arrogancy, and the evil way, and the froward mouth, do I hate."},{"ref":"Psalm 147:11","text":"The LORD taketh pleasure in them that fear him, in those that hope in his mercy."},{"ref":"Ecclesiastes 12:13","text":"Let us hear the conclusion of the whole matter: Fear God, and keep his commandments: for this is the whole duty of man."},{"ref":"Isaiah 66:2","text":"For all those things hath mine hand made, and all those things have been, saith the LORD: but to this man will I look, even to him that is poor and of a contrite spirit, and trembleth at my word."},{"ref":"Hebrews 12:28-29","text":"Wherefore we receiving a kingdom which cannot be moved, let us have grace, whereby we may serve God acceptably with reverence and godly fear: For our God is a consuming fire."},{"ref":"Psalm 111:10","text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom: a good understanding have all they that do his commandments: his praise endureth for ever."},{"ref":"Acts 9:31","text":"Then had the churches rest throughout all Judaea and Galilee and Samaria, and were edified; and walking in the fear of the Lord, and in the comfort of the Holy Ghost, were multiplied."},{"ref":"Philippians 2:12-13","text":"Wherefore, my beloved, as ye have always obeyed, not as in my presence only, but now much more in my absence, work out your own salvation with fear and trembling. For it is God which worketh in you both to will and to do of his good pleasure."}],"reflect":["Where do I fear people more than God?","Do I treat God as casual, or do I approach Him with awe and love?","What would a reverent life look like this week?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Teach me to fear You","x":"Holy God, You are great and greatly to be praised. Forgive me for treating You lightly, for fearing people more than I fear You, and for living as though You do not see. Give me a true and deep reverence for who You are.\n\nUnite my heart to fear Your name. Teach me Your way, O Lord, that I may walk in Your truth. Let the fear of the Lord keep me from evil and draw me to wisdom. Free me from the fear of man and the fear of tomorrow. Thank You that Your perfect love casts out all fear. In Jesus' name, Amen."}],"declare":["The fear of the Lord is my treasure.","I will not fear what people can do to me.","I will serve God with reverence and awe.","God is both holy and loving, and I trust Him."],"care":""},{"id":"return","title":"The Second Coming and Resurrection","icon":"cross","words":"second coming return rapture resurrection end times tribulation antichrist rapture last days judgment day revelation","intro":"Jesus rose from the dead, and the Bible says He will return in glory. The resurrection is the foundation of Christian hope: it proves who Jesus is and promises that those who belong to Him will also be raised. Christians hold different views about the order of the final events, but all agree on the main call: be ready.","points":["If Christ has not been raised, our faith is in vain; but now Christ is risen from the dead (1 Corinthians 15:14, 20).","The Lord Himself will descend from heaven, and the dead in Christ will rise first (1 Thessalonians 4:16-17).","No one knows the day or hour, so keep watch (Matthew 24:36, 42).","He will make all things new (Revelation 21:5).","Live holy and godly lives, looking forward to the day of God (2 Peter 3:11-13).","Our labor in the Lord is not in vain (1 Corinthians 15:58)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:3-4","text":"For I delivered unto you first of all that which I also received, how that Christ died for our sins according to the scriptures; And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures:"},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:20-22","text":"But now is Christ risen from the dead, and become the firstfruits of them that slept. For since by man came death, by man came also the resurrection of the dead. For as in Adam all die, even so in Christ shall all be made alive."},{"ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:16-17","text":"For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Christ shall rise first: Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord."},{"ref":"Matthew 24:36","text":"But of that day and hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels of heaven, but my Father only."},{"ref":"Matthew 24:42-44","text":"Watch therefore: for ye know not what hour your Lord doth come. But know this, that if the goodman of the house had known in what watch the thief would come, he would have watched, and would not have suffered his house to be broken up. Therefore be ye also ready: for in such an hour as ye think not the Son of man cometh."},{"ref":"Revelation 21:5","text":"And he that sat upon the throne said, Behold, I make all things new. And he said unto me, Write: for these words are true and faithful."},{"ref":"Acts 1:11","text":"Which also said, Ye men of Galilee, why stand ye gazing up into heaven? this same Jesus, which is taken up from you into heaven, shall so come in like manner as ye have seen him go into heaven."},{"ref":"Titus 2:13","text":"Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of the great God and our Saviour Jesus Christ;"},{"ref":"Luke 24:5-6","text":"And as they were afraid, and bowed down their faces to the earth, they said unto them, Why seek ye the living among the dead? He is not here, but is risen: remember how he spake unto you when he was yet in Galilee,"},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:58","text":"Therefore, my beloved brethren, be ye stedfast, unmoveable, always abounding in the work of the Lord, forasmuch as ye know that your labour is not in vain in the Lord."}],"reflect":["If Jesus returned today, what would I want to have done?","Am I more curious about timelines than ready in my heart?","Who needs me to share the hope of the resurrection?"],"prayers":[{"t":"Come, Lord Jesus","x":"Lord Jesus, You rose from the dead and You will return. I thank You for the sure hope of the resurrection. Help me to live ready: faithful in small things, honest with You, forgiving others and telling the good news. Keep me from fear and from distraction.\n\nWhen the world is shaking, anchor my heart in You. Make me watchful and joyful. Use me while it is still day. And when You come, let You find me faithful. Even so, come, Lord Jesus. Amen."}],"declare":["Christ is risen, and I will rise with Him.","My Redeemer lives.","My labor in the Lord is not in vain.","I am ready and I am watching for His return."],"care":""},{"id":"fasting","title":"Fasting and Persistent Prayer","icon":"flame","words":"fasting fast persistent prayer intercession pray without ceasing travail breakthrough midnight","intro":"Throughout Scripture, God's people fasted and prayed with persistence in times of need, repentance and decision. Jesus assumed His followers would fast (\"when you fast\"). Fasting does not twist God's arm; it humbles us, focuses our hearts and makes room to listen.","points":["Jesus said, \"When thou fastest,\" and taught us to do it quietly, not to be seen by people (Matthew 6:16-18).","Persistent prayer: pray and do not lose heart (Luke 18:1-8).","Pray without ceasing, and give thanks in all circumstances (1 Thessalonians 5:17-18).","The fast that pleases God includes justice, mercy and caring for the poor (Isaiah 58:6-7).","The church prayed earnestly when Peter was in prison, and God answered (Acts 12:5-7).","Ask, seek and knock (Matthew 7:7-8)."],"scriptures":[{"ref":"Matthew 6:16-18","text":"Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward. But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face; That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret: and thy Father, which seeth in secret, shall reward thee openly."},{"ref":"Luke 18:1-8","text":"And he spake a parable unto them to this end, that men ought always to pray, and not to faint; Saying, There was in a city a judge, which feared not God, neither regarded man: And there was a widow in that city; and she came unto him, saying, Avenge me of mine adversary. And he would not for a while: but afterward he said within himself, Though I fear not God, nor regard man; Yet because this widow troubleth me, I will avenge her, lest by her continual coming she weary me. And the Lord said, Hear what the unjust judge saith. And shall not God avenge his own elect, which cry day and night unto him, though he bear long with them? I tell you that he will avenge them speedily. Nevertheless when the Son of man cometh, shall he find faith on the earth?"},{"ref":"1 Thessalonians 5:17-18","text":"Pray without ceasing. In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you."},{"ref":"Isaiah 58:6-7","text":"Is not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke? Is it not to deal thy bread to the hungry, and that thou bring the poor that are cast out to thy house? when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him; and that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh?"},{"ref":"Acts 12:5-7","text":"Peter therefore was kept in prison: but prayer was made without ceasing of the church unto God for him. And when Herod would have brought him forth, the same night Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, bound with two chains: and the keepers before the door kept the prison. And, behold, the angel of the Lord came upon him, and a light shined in the prison: and he smote Peter on the side, and raised him up, saying, Arise up quickly. And his chains fell off from his hands."},{"ref":"Matthew 7:7-8","text":"Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you: For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened."},{"ref":"Joel 2:12","text":"Therefore also now, saith the LORD, turn ye even to me with all your heart, and with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning:"},{"ref":"Ezra 8:23","text":"So we fasted and besought our God for this: and he was intreated of us."},{"ref":"Daniel 9:3","text":"And I set my face unto the Lord God, to seek by prayer and supplications, with fasting, and sackcloth, and ashes:"},{"ref":"James 5:16","text":"Confess your faults one to another, and pray one for another, that ye may be healed. The effectual fervent prayer of a righteous man availeth much."}],"reflect":["What do I want to seek God about most, and why?","How can I fast wisely (check health first and do not starve)?","Who can I pray with regularly?"],"prayers":[{"t":"A prayer during a fast","x":"Father, I set this time apart to seek You. I put aside food (or: distractions) so that I can hear You more clearly. I humble myself under Your mighty hand. Show me what You want to show me. Search my heart, cleanse me and renew my hunger for You.\n\nI bring before You (name your need). I ask, I seek and I knock, and I will not give up. Strengthen me, because the flesh is weak. Let this time draw me closer to You and make me more like Jesus. Thank You that You hear and answer. In Jesus' name, Amen."}],"declare":["The Lord hears me when I call.","I will not lose heart: I will pray and not give up.","Those who seek Him find Him.","God rewards those who earnestly seek Him."],"care":"Fasting from food is not suitable for everyone: if you are pregnant, ill, diabetic, on medication or under 18, talk to a doctor first, or fast from something else, such as screens."}];
